SUPERMARKET SALES ANALYSIS
Internship Data Analytics Project Report


Submitted by
Arijit Paul

BCA – Data Analytics / Machine Learning
Academic / Internship Project
2026


1. Abstract
This project presents an end-to-end analysis of a supermarket sales dataset containing 500 transactions. The source data was supplied as a PDF and was converted into a structured CSV using Python and PyMuPDF. The extracted data was cleaned and validated using Pandas, with Sales calculated from Quantity × Unit Price. The project then analyzes sales performance by product, category, branch, customer type, gender, payment method and month. Interactive visualizations were created with Plotly and an interactive Streamlit dashboard was developed. The results were also independently compared with the benchmark results stated in the project manual.
2. Introduction
Retail transaction data contains useful information for understanding sales performance, customer behavior and payment patterns. A structured analytical workflow helps transform raw transaction records into reliable business information. This project demonstrates that workflow using Python, Pandas and interactive visualization tools.
3. Problem Statement
The objective is to analyze supermarket sales transactions and identify useful information about products, branches, categories, customers, payment methods and ratings. The project also requires data-quality checking, calculation of sales values, summary statistics and meaningful visualizations.
4. Objectives
Extract the supplied supermarket transaction table from PDF format.
Convert the extracted records into a structured CSV dataset.
Clean and validate dates, numeric values, categories and identifiers.
Calculate Sales using Quantity × Unit Price.
Analyze sales by product, branch, category, customer type and payment method.
Study customer ratings and monthly sales trends.
Create interactive charts and a Streamlit dashboard.
Verify the project-manual benchmark results against independently calculated results.
5. Dataset Description
The source contains 500 supermarket sales transactions. The extracted schema contains 13 fields: Invoice ID, Date, Branch, City, Customer Type, Gender, Product, Category, Quantity, Unit Price, Payment, Rating and Sales.
