11. Dashboard
The Streamlit dashboard provides KPI cards and interactive filters for Branch, City, Category, Product, Customer Type, Gender, Payment and Date. Dashboard tabs cover overview, products/categories, customers/payments, and data quality/manual verification. Plotly is used for interactive charts.
12. Business Insights
Branch C (Mumbai) records the highest sales in the extracted dataset.
Beverages is the highest-sales category.
Cheese, Coffee and Shampoo are the three highest-sales products.
Members account for 296 of 500 transactions, while Normal customers account for 204.
UPI is the most-used payment method with 127 transactions.
April records the highest monthly sales in the extracted period; July has comparatively few source transactions.
13. Recommendations
Monitor stock availability for high-sales products such as Cheese, Coffee and Shampoo.
Study the product/store mix associated with Branch C and identify practices that may be useful for other branches.
Continue supporting UPI while retaining alternative payment methods because usage is distributed across the available options.
Use rating analysis to identify products or service areas that may require improvement.
Consider the difference between Member and Normal average transaction values when designing membership offers.
14. Project Structure
The repository contains the Jupyter Notebook, Streamlit dashboard, reusable source modules, requirements file, tests, source PDFs, processed CSV files and analytical verification outputs.
15. Testing
Automated project tests were executed successfully for extraction shape and invoice IDs, data cleaning and Sales arithmetic, manual benchmark verification and key analytical results. Python source files were also syntax-compiled successfully. A browser-level Streamlit launch could not be completed in the build environment because Streamlit was not installed there and external package installation was unavailable; the dependency is listed in requirements.txt for normal local execution.
16. Limitations
The source dataset does not contain profit, cost, inventory, discount or customer-ID fields.
The source PDF is treated as the authoritative transaction source.
July contains relatively few transactions, limiting direct full-month seasonal interpretation.
The dashboard requires the listed Python dependencies to be installed in the execution environment.
17. Future Scope
Add profit-margin analysis if cost data becomes available.
Add inventory and stock-out analysis if inventory data is available.
Add customer-level segmentation if customer identifiers become available.
Deploy the Streamlit dashboard to a cloud platform.
Add automated scheduled refresh when a continuously updated data source is available.
18. Conclusion
The project demonstrates a complete data analytics pipeline from PDF extraction to validated data, exploratory analysis, interactive visualization and dashboard presentation. The final dataset contains 500 validated transactions, and the principal benchmark values in the project manual were reproduced independently from the data. The resulting notebook, dashboard and supporting files provide a reproducible internship-level submission.
